      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While yes it would be great to have more 2FA options, the root problem is the logins not being remembered. Either the 2FA needs to remain on the reconginsed device or the whole login needs to be remembered. Currently its so painful because of how much we need to login.\nWith the amount of server issues vrchat is having we at least need the 2FA to be remembered because auto filling passwords already exists, albeit still painful in vr its better than having to take the headset off entirely to try and input a 2FA code while vr is running and not having a static camera to type it in.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "61e4b641ac8d6044dc92c41a",
      "author": {
        "_id": "61e4b48ef5558742748e550b",
        "alias": "Azure Herring",
        "aliasID": "6618bca0e5d26962aa055f99",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/e9f2b1090c1f1e510a3f9541dbb750a3.png",
        "created": "2022-01-17T00:13:02.908Z",
        "name": "Shiny~∗",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-01-17T00:20:17.820Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "604a87a00fc80c3d981b42db",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would really like to see Authentication keys (e.g. Yubikey, Google Titan) as an option in addition to a One-time-code generator Authentication apps (Authy, Google Authenticator). \nI'm always worried about my phone dying or failing and having issues recovering my codes in the app. I've also had some codes unsync somehow in the Google Auth. app. It's happened to me twice over three years of use :(",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "640e5610d34a3045273ec655",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5fb908aead7a8d6236ca6b4a",
        "alias": "Jittery Macaw",
        "aliasID": "65e0d15aa6e3ea79dd7a6280",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/17850f250f5dc3505545e7861e779d76.png",
        "created": "2020-11-21T12:31:42.932Z",
        "name": "Ecoleaf",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-03-12T22:45:36.762Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "604a87a00fc80c3d981b42db",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I definitely agree!\n\nI believe that security keys such as the Yubikey 5 series is much more secure overall when using FIDO 2FA or FIDO2.\n\nEven though Time-Based One-Time-Passwords are good enough, it leaves flexability to other security keys off the table that do not support such VRChat's current 2FA model.\n\nAs for logins not being remembered, even though it could be improved in the future, this is a matter of convenient vs security. To me, I use VRChat's TOTP 2FA system, and that is still not convenient. However I choose to go through the extra effort to ensure I have good security for my account. I would happily do the same if there was FIDO2 / YubiKey support. \n\nAt least with a Yubikey all I would need to mostly do is press on the Yubikey when in PCVR. This definitely beats rushing to copy the code down in a middle of a VR session.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-11T21:12:00.805Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VR does not lend itself well to using Authy for 2FA; I suggest adding an option to use USB authentication keys as an alternative for easier interaction and to remove the need for keyboard input while in VR.\nSee: https://www.yubico.com/",
